! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node for control-map node R3 (Belief update): R3 solves how observations change belief without either overwriting it or letting it become immovable: the roster places **“Belief update”** in BELIEVE (`p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:18`; control-stage numbering).

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L5 from the twenty-node problem dossiers; it exists so @why edges from mechanism patterns have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: R3 solves how observations change belief without either overwriting it or letting it become immovable: the roster places **“Belief update”** in BELIEVE (`p4ng/empirics-futon/control-stages.edn:18`; control-stage numbering). The operational contract requires prediction error, precision weighting, variational free energy, and an update step all to be computed by name (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:80-106`; contract R3). The catalogue prescribes moving belief toward observation only as far as learning rate and channel trust allow, while **“never letting that uncertainty fall below a floor”** (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:198`; catalogue R3). The registry writes the reduction as `mu <- mu + alpha Pi eps`, importing prior belief, precision, error, and step size (`holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn:104-107`; control-stage R3). R3 therefore solves controlled revision: the direction comes from error, the amount from learning rate and trust, and retained uncertainty prevents false certainty. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, R3, The problem it solves)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.

  + BECAUSE:
    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.
    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-r1-r3-r3a-batch3.md, section "## R3 — Belief update", subsection "The problem it solves".
